  "findings": [
    "Physical velocity maps exactly and invertibly into three Cell3 half-step traversal rates.",
    "The address coupling W and physical response G_phase are strictly positive definite.",
    "Every nonzero unit-sphere direction therefore has positive raw phase cost; no null direction exists.",
    "The raw directional phase cost is antipodally even and bounded by the eigenvalues of G_phase.",
    "Self-indexing supplies the occupied projective direction and the exact direction-dependent normalization beta(u).",
    "The normalized phase scalar equals ordinary kinetic energy per unit mass, v^2/2, in every direction.",
    "Along Earth-CMB traversal, 293.0619367 GJ/kg of raw phase scalar normalizes to 68.3806433 GJ/kg of kinetic energy.",
    "Linear inertia is the resistance to changing the normalized coherent a/b/c traversal-rate state.",
    "Momentum is the first derivative and inertial mass is the curvature scale of this normalized energy state.",
    "The rotating-mass lateral response is the residual mixed term between Earth baseline traversal and local traversal.",
    "The supplied lateral coefficient expresses approximately 6.5873e-11 of the full normalized mixed interaction.",
    "The continuous rate-energy derivation is closed; exclusive node or plane-crossing localization remains a separate composition rule."
  ],
